+# DDoS / Availability Runbook (summary)
+
+Purpose
+- Provide steps to mitigate large-scale DDoS or availability incidents and failover to safety-critical control plane.
+
+1) Detection
+ - Alert if >X RPS sustained, response latencies spike, or error rates exceed threshold.
+ - Use WAF & ingress metrics + Prometheus alerts.
+
+2) Immediate mitigation
+ - Enable WAF rules (block offending IP blocks or geo regions).
+ - Apply ingress rate-limiting (increase limits gradually for critical services).
+ - Scale safety-critical deployments (receipt-signer, approver, staged-autonomy) to minimum healthy replicas.
+ - Route non-critical traffic to maintenance page / degrade gracefully.
+
+3) Failover control plane
+ - If control plane (e.g., external approver) is attacked, switch to offline A2A fallback for edge sites (fetchtokens).
+ - Enable fail-open for low-risk webhooks if documented risk accepted: set FAIL_ON_ERROR=false.
+
+4) Recovery & validation
+ - Run replay checks for any allowed operations during fail-open.
+ - Reconcile Rekor and cosign logs; validate that no unsigned model deployments occurred.
+ - Postmortem with root cause, list of impacted artifacts and remediation.
+
+5) Post-incident
+ - Rotate keys (KMS) if suspected compromise and re-encrypt S3 objects (use aws_kms_rotate helper).
+ - Update WAF rules for long-term protection.
+
